<h3>About AlphaDict</h3>

<p><b>version:</b> 1.4.1<br/>
AlphaDict by joni lee (li liqiong) &lt;joni_lee@outlook.com&gt;.<br/>
<b>website:</b> prajna.top</p>

<p>It's a lightweight, open-source dictionary software with an open dictionary format, so that you can make your own dictionary.</p>

<p>You can download the software, code and dicts, and get information from the URLs below:</p>

<ul>
<li>sourceforge: <a href="http://sourceforge.net/projects/alphadict">sourceforge.net/projects/alphadict</a></li>
<li>github: <a href="https://github.com/kartorz/AlphaDict">github.com/kartorz/AlphaDict</a></li>
<li>wiki: <a href="https://github.com/kartorz/AlphaDict/wiki">github.com/kartorz/AlphaDict/wiki</a></li>
<li>netdisk: <a href="http://pan.baidu.com/s/1dD9v12D">pan.baidu.com/s/1dD9v12D</a></li>
</ul>

<h3>Dictionary Format</h3>

<p>AlphaDict has a custom dictionary format including a back-end inner format (<tt>doc/dictionary_inner.pdf</tt>) and a front-end xml format (<tt>doc/front-end_format.xml</tt>).</p>

<p>Usually, a user should edit the "front-end" xml, then use <tt>AldConvert(.exe)</tt> to convert it. More detail about dictionaries, see the "README" doc or the "wiki".</p>

<h3>Dictionary Selection</h3>

<p>AlphaDict supports a variety of languages. It selects a dict according to language instead of input text. It checks dicts one by one from top to bottom of the dict list, until it finds a dict that fits the language on the "Dictionary page".</p>

<p>A user can choose source and destination language on the "Dictionary page", and change the order of dicts in the list on the "Setting page". AlphaDict will choose a dict according to the change of settings.</p>

<p>For example:</p>

<ul>
<li><tt>"any" --&gt; "any"</tt>: select the first dict, definitely.</li>
<li><tt>"any" --&gt; "chinese"</tt>: select the first dict whose destination language is "chinese" or "any".</li>
<li><tt>"english" --&gt; "chinese"</tt>: select the first dict whose source language is "english" or "any", and whose destination language is "chinese" or "any".</li>
</ul>

<p>The "any" value of a language can match any language (in other words, it is not specified).</p>

<h3>Capture Word of Screen</h3>

<p>AlphaDict supports two capture methods, a shortcut key to enable/disable this function, and auto closing of the "Capture Word Dialog".</p>

<h4>Capture Methods</h4>

<ul>
<li><b>Mouse Selection</b>: select text by mouse &mdash; press the left button of the mouse, move the mouse, then release the button; or double click the left mouse button for some applications, like IE or firefox. AlphaDict will capture the selected word and translate it. Supports almost all applications, like IE, Adobe pdf, firefox, etc.</li>
<li><b>Clipboard</b>: copy the text to the clipboard. AlphaDict will listen for clipboard changes, get this text and translate it.</li>
</ul>

<p>A user can change the settings on the "Dict Setting Page".</p>

<h4>Shortcut Key</h4>

<p>It's annoying when AlphaDict pops the Capture Word Dialog always. So AlphaDict provides a shortcut key: you can disable or enable the capture function alternately. The default shortcut key is <tt>Ctrl + Alt + G</tt> &mdash; G is the key, not the capital letter.</p>

<h4>How to Close the Capture Word Dialog</h4>

<ul>
<li><b>ESC key</b>: if the dialog can't be closed, the user should click the "Capture Word Dialog" first (focus on the dialog), then press the ESC key.</li>
<li><b>Mouse click outside of the dialog</b>: currently AlphaDict doesn't support win64 applications and some other applications, like IE. If the dialog can't be closed, the user should click the "Capture Word Dialog" first (focus on the dialog), then click outside of the dialog.</li>
<li><b>Auto close (3s)</b>: the user can enable/disable "autoclose" on the "Dict Setting Page". When the mouse is over this dialog, "autoclose" will be disabled.</li>
</ul>

<h3>System Setting</h3>

<p>The following settings require restarting the application to become valid.</p>

<ul>
<li>UI Language</li>
<li>Font</li>
<li>Font Size</li>
<li>Restore to Default Setting</li>
</ul>

<h3>FAQ</h3>

<h4>How to close a sub window, e.g. 'Setting', 'Help'?</h4>

<p>Activate the window again from the tool bar.</p>

<h4>How to prevent a repeated selection in emacs?</h4>

<p>Turn on 'Non-repeat selection' on the 'Setting page'.</p>
